  "$comment": "Every upstream file the language-pack builders download, pinned. `sha256` and `bytes` were measured with `sha256sum` / `stat -c %s` over scripts/language-packs/.cache/ and re-verified by re-downloading each raw.githubusercontent.com URL at the pinned commit. A download whose digest does not match is refused, so a poisoned or silently-updated upstream fails the build instead of reaching a learner's machine. Updating an upstream is a manual edit here: download the new file, run sha256sum on it, and paste both numbers in. `commits` records where the /<sha>/ path segments in the builders come from — re-query with `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/commits/master --jq .sha`. Kaikki has no commit ids; its extracts are re-cut periodically, so its digests are dated snapshots and a mismatch there usually means the dump moved, not that anything is wrong.",
